WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:01.810
- I couldn't help but notice,

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.640
first of all, I'm such a fan.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.473
So excited.
- Thank you.

00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:05.580
Thank you so much.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.180
- But I also noticed you have like a,

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.830
is this special, this necklace
thing that's going on?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.960
- This is me and my late
daughter, Bobbi Kristina.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.100
- Oh! And then there are these little,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.710
is it quartz around it or what?

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.810
Is there--
- Yeah, little beads

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.316
that her sister gave me.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:19.230
- Oh!

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.780
- Our daughter, Hendrix.
- Our daughter, Hendricks,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.950
made it for me to go on tour with.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.380
- Oh my gosh, I love that!

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.790
I didn't even notice there
was the picture on that.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.380
I was talking about the
beads and so I was just like,

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.990
oh, are you into like stones and stuff?

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.240
I am quartz nerd.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.447
That's so beautiful.
- Thank you.

00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:33.410
- And you carry that around,
that's such a beautiful thing.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.550
Y'all look so nice.
- Thank you.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.079
- Like ready for a photo
shoot (indistinct).

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.270
I was like.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.570
So we're celebrating Rad Momma's Week.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.403
I'm sure that she is an awesome mama,

00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:43.236
two take kiddos.
- Oh yes! Yes.

00:00:43.236 --> 00:00:44.350
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Totally. Totally.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.180
- Is it fun? Is it a crazy house?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.830
- It's not a crazy house.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.000
It's a very loving house.
- Mine's crazy.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.921
- It's not crazy to him.
It's definitely crazy to me.

00:00:51.921 --> 00:00:54.840
- I was gonna say it's crazy
to me. It's loving and crazy.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.190
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.783
- It's crazy to her, but not to me.

00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:00.230
(Alicia chuckling)
(audience laughing)

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.063
- Yes.

00:01:01.063 --> 00:01:03.020
- So what's your favorite
part of being a mama?

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.853
- Oh, man!

00:01:03.853 --> 00:01:07.330
Just watching these little
humans become their personalities

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.295
and them big selves.

00:01:09.295 --> 00:01:11.260
And then it just takes you
back to when you were a child

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.450
and all the things you loved

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.273
and watching it through their eyes.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:15.183
- You like re-experience it.

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:16.490
- You re-experience it!

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.980
That is the gift of being
a mother, absolutely.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.330
- Yeah. I agree.
- It's a beautiful thing.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.170
- I agree.
- Yeah.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.720
- So wait, is it true that,
you know, when you were young,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.730
you heard music in your head all the time?

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:26.563
Is that true?
- Yeah.

00:01:26.563 --> 00:01:29.000
I used to bang my head against the--

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.700
- So I used to like write all the time,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.750
but you just heard stuff constantly.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.400
- I just heard music constantly.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.570
And I would bang my head

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.910
and didn't know why I would
bang my head against the wall

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:39.743
all the time.

00:01:39.743 --> 00:01:41.930
And the teachers used to tell my mother,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.970
you know, he's banging
his head again and--

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:45.803
- Yeah,

00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:46.636
that would kinda scare me.
- Later on we found out

00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:47.860
it was just music.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:48.693
- Yeah.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.570
For some reason, like why I got into music

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.470
was I had a hard time communicating

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.170
and it helped me like process it.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.750
My mom was like, maybe
you should write it down.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.830
'Cause I would bottle up.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:01.430
And I think the music

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:02.660
and everything that I
would hear in my head

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.730
and all these thoughts, I
had a hard time getting out,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.670
and music was helpful for me in that area.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:07.830
Was that like that for you?

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.020
- Yes. Lots of talent shows.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.570
I did lots of talent shows
everywhere in Boston.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.170
And I think that's what got me to realize

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.620
that this was music.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.150
- Yeah. And that expression feels so good.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.270
Yeah. That it's not only
up here. It's out here.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.150
- Yeah.
- We thank you for it.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.706
We enjoy it out here so.
- Thank you.

00:02:26.706 --> 00:02:28.658
(audience applauding)

00:02:28.658 --> 00:02:30.000
- So is it true?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.410
I heard that you were
the one that talked him

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.210
like out of his like jitters

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.670
when you and Whitney were getting married.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.503
- Yes.
- Is that true?

00:02:36.503 --> 00:02:37.336
- Yes. Yes.
- Yes, she was the one.

00:02:37.336 --> 00:02:41.320
- How full circle is that?
- I know.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.060
- So wait, so you were,
everyone is nervous, right?

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:44.893
Like when you're about

00:02:44.893 --> 00:02:45.726
to put the ring.
- That's what I say,

00:02:45.726 --> 00:02:46.559
everyone is nervous.

00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:47.845
- And if they're not, you're weird.

00:02:47.845 --> 00:02:49.410
- I was extra nervous.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.510
- It's a terrifying kinda thing,

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.990
that you're like, it's a, you know,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.830
big step.
- It's a big deal.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.070
It's a big step in your life. Yeah.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.140
- I Just love that you
were like, you got this!

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:56.973
- Yeah. I was like, get out!
- And then

00:02:56.973 --> 00:02:58.760
y'all end up married like years later.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.866
- Isn't that crazy? I know.
- I know.

00:03:00.866 --> 00:03:02.770
- I know. It's amazing.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.230
It's the timing of everything

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.640
and why things are meant to be.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.580
But for sure, I was there. I was a friend.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.710
And by then all of his groomsmen

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.880
and his brother could not
get him out the bathroom.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.440
So I was like, listen, we are
getting this show on the road.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.290
You know we're here and this
is happening and you know--

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.880
- Oh, they couldn't get
you out of the room?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.303
Like you had serious chills.

00:03:22.303 --> 00:03:24.083
- I had real, that's what
I was telling you, Kelly.

00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:26.290
- Okay. My God, I thought
you meant just like,

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.227
you know, everybody's
like me and I'm not--

00:03:27.227 --> 00:03:29.648
- No, I locked myself in a bathroom!

00:03:29.648 --> 00:03:31.060
- Oh my God!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.525
Okay. Okay.
- Yes.

00:03:32.525 --> 00:03:33.830
- [Alicia] So it was fun for us.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.910
- I wasn't gonna come out for anybody.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.690
- Did she know about this?

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.530
- I think everybody knew
about it (chuckles).

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.310
- Oh my gosh, that's terrifying!

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.143
So you're the one that ended up--

00:03:42.143 --> 00:03:43.710
- She was like, he better
get out that bathroom!

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.830
- He better get out of that bathroom.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.290
- But for some reason,
yeah, I came to the door,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.670
I knocked on it, and I was
talking to him through the door.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.280
And then finally, he like
peeked it a little bit

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.517
and I got in, you know?
- Yeah.

00:03:54.517 --> 00:03:56.510
- And it was like, let me in, let me in.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.560
Everything's gonna be okay.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:00.774
And for some reason, he listens to me.

00:04:00.774 --> 00:04:03.010
(Alicia and Bobby laughing)

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.360
And he eventually came out the bathroom

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.540
and went down that aisle. Yeah.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.610
But it is ironic

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.770
that it was us again
meeting in life later on

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.603
and he would be my husband.

00:04:10.603 --> 00:04:13.003
- Yeah. That's so great! I love that!

00:04:13.003 --> 00:04:13.920
(audience clapping)

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.690
It's like a really interesting,
cool romantic comedy.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.523
- Yeah (laughs).
- I would watch that movie.

00:04:18.523 --> 00:04:19.508
(Alicia laughing)

00:04:19.508 --> 00:04:20.452
If you were in it.

00:04:20.452 --> 00:04:23.443
That was a look at their
show, "Biography: Bobby Brown".

00:04:23.443 --> 00:04:26.940
And you're both really honest
about Bobby's struggles

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:27.773
during the documentary.

00:04:27.773 --> 00:04:28.970
I think that's really important.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.890
I don't think that you
should do that kinda thing

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:31.730
unless you are honest,

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.100
but it's got to be really hard

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.020
'cause we're already
under so much scrutiny

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.500
in the public eye as it is.
- Yeah.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.560
- So was that really hard
or was it also therapeutic?

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.510
- It was definitely therapeutic for me,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.750
having to relive all of the ups and downs.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:47.993
I think for me,

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.430
I needed to clean out all of the cobwebs

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.670
in order to move forward in life.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.960
And move forward with my family, my wife,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.623
and to move forward just for my wellbeing.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.560
It was definitely a need.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:09.270
- I think that's what, people
that are like not for therapy,

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.570
you know, they're like, ugh,
I don't believe in therapy.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.050
I'm like, it's just a healthy process

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.910
with someone who's outside of
your circle. Won't judge you.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:15.810
It's one of those things for me.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.850
And I feel like that's the same way,

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.140
sometimes almost in an interview,

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:19.950
I feel that way, 'cause I'm very open

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.830
and it's a way to kind of express
something that's going on.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.120
And I love that.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.910
I think it helps you kind
of work through stuff.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.550
I think it's a very healthy
way of dealing with things.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.250
- Definitely.
- Yeah.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.550
- But so what's the biggest thing

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.700
that people, you feel like
get wrong about Bobby's life?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.590
- That he's a big, old meany or something.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:36.429
He's like the biggest--
- Wait,

00:05:36.429 --> 00:05:37.262
people think you're mean?

00:05:37.262 --> 00:05:40.470
- Well, you know, like
he's not a happy soul.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:44.450
He's this like amazing teddy
bear of a dad and a husband,

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:47.850
and he really cries
over any and everything,

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:49.615
but in the sweetest way.
- Come on now!

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.490
- He was like, no, wait!
- In the sweetest way!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.593
He's very sentimental
about things and you know--

00:05:54.593 --> 00:05:56.360
- I don't cry over everything.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.193
- Yeah.

00:05:57.193 --> 00:06:01.981
- I mean, just like commercials.
Like commercials get me.

00:06:01.981 --> 00:06:03.080
- Commercials get me!

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.600
You have a heart!
- Oh my God!

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:06.730
- God! When they get together,
a long lost love on it.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.330
Yeah, they want you cry!
- Oh yes!

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.410
- Or any of those commercials

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:10.818
with all the animals that are dying

00:06:10.818 --> 00:06:12.519
and seeing those
(indistinct) is killing you.

00:06:12.519 --> 00:06:13.920
- Those are terrible.
- Yeah.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:14.790
I cry too.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.720
I think that your
heartless if you don't cry.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:17.980
Aint nothing wrong with that.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:18.813
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:06:18.813 --> 00:06:21.240
- I feel like the older we
get, we get more emotional too.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.980
I feel like that.
- I feel like that for sure.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.813
- Yeah.
- Absolutely.

00:06:23.813 --> 00:06:26.220
- Yes! (laughs) We got an amen.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.790
So what do you think, Bobby,

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.713
like the biggest misconception
that people have about you?

00:06:31.792 --> 00:06:33.980
- That I'm a bad boy.
- Yeah.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:38.950
- That the bad boy image
is taken from off stage.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.330
When I'm on stage, I'm a bad boy,

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:45.420
but when I'm off stage,
you know, I'm just Bobby.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.253
You know?
- Yeah.

00:06:46.253 --> 00:06:47.086
[Audience] Aww!

00:06:47.086 --> 00:06:48.346
- I love y'all today.

00:06:48.346 --> 00:06:50.450
(audience applauding)

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:53.043
I mean, maybe I'm not one of
pop culture in that sense.

00:06:53.043 --> 00:06:54.530
I don't like read everything or whatever,

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.350
but I've never, and I've
been a fan since I was a kid,

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.025
so I've never gotten that from you.

00:06:58.025 --> 00:06:59.683
Like as a fan, like I've always known

00:06:59.683 --> 00:07:01.590
that you're just a talented dude.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:04.263
And like, I've never ever
gotten that vibe from you.

00:07:04.263 --> 00:07:05.096
- Thank you.

00:07:05.096 --> 00:07:06.697
- 'Cause most people that are
projecting that image on stage

00:07:06.697 --> 00:07:10.610
and like doing stuff, they're
like fun as hell after show.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:11.820
And you're hanging with
them and they're fun.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.750
And then it's like part of what we do

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.780
is kind of you put a show on for people.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.706
- Yes.
- So yeah, I never got that.

00:07:17.706 --> 00:07:18.881
I might've missed on that.
- Well, thank you.

00:07:18.881 --> 00:07:20.560
I'm glad you didn't get it.
- No. Yeah.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.390
Okay. So there's a
moment in the documentary

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.240
where Bobby goes to the graves
of Whitney and his daughter.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.683
So why was that important
for you to put in this?

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.720
- Because I hadn't been there before.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.660
- Oh, really?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.980
- No, I hadn't. I don't like grave sites.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:39.830
So I hadn't been to my
mother's, my father's,

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.470
or anybody else's, my grandmother's.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:46.360
So I just decided that, you
know, I gotta grow up here

00:07:47.487 --> 00:07:50.970
and just go ahead and go
by and leave some flowers,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.713
and make my peace with,
you know, with them both.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.913
- I love that.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.858
I mean, I guess when you
were talking about that,

00:08:00.858 --> 00:08:03.150
I was like, I don't really
visit things like that too.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.700
I think that's not for everyone.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.970
My sister and I always have this talk too.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:10.010
Like funerals are hard for everyone,

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.890
but like some of us are, even
if you don't know the person,

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.840
like I will be there, I'm such an empath.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.730
I take on all that loss

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:19.660
and I become like a
distraction at a funeral.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.780
Like 'cause I'm just
like sobbing. It's weird!

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.530
And my sister and I are the same way.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:27.420
And I can't handle like grave
sites. It's just too much.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.900
'Cause I don't wanna
focus so much on the loss,

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.530
I'd rather focus on the
life that we've lived,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.330
and like the good times.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.163
- We agree.

00:08:35.163 --> 00:08:37.700
- Like I don't think that that's
necessarily a healthy move

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.410
for everyone, you know,
to be able to do that.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.049
But I think that that closure is nice.

00:08:42.049 --> 00:08:44.120
- That closure is beautiful.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.330
- 'Cause it's a lot of loss.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.310
And that's a lot on a heart.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.540
- Yes it is.
- Yeah.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.841
Well, you've now reunited
with New Edition for a tour.

00:08:52.841 --> 00:08:54.174
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:08:54.174 --> 00:08:55.763
So how is that going?

00:08:55.763 --> 00:08:58.135
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:08:58.135 --> 00:08:58.968
- We...

00:08:58.968 --> 00:08:59.801
- [Alicia] Look at that photo.

00:08:59.801 --> 00:09:01.070
- [Kelly] This is amazing!

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:03.710
- We actually just finished the tour.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.100
We did 30-city tour

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.375
and it was everything
that I expected it to be.

00:09:09.375 --> 00:09:10.208
- Oh my God!

00:09:10.208 --> 00:09:13.500
- It was a lot of hard
work, a lot of dancing,

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.580
a lot of laughing, a lot of joking around.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:20.890
Just the camaraderie between all six of us

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.350
is just so much fun.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.950
It was like camp.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:26.147
It was like--
- And isn't it different

00:09:26.147 --> 00:09:27.670
'cause you're all like older now?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.820
So that's like the thing I love.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.780
Like when I run into people,

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.180
like even I've been in
the industry 20 years,

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.740
and I run into someone,
I'm like, oh my God,

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.160
when I knew you, I was just
such a different human.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.110
I feel like, you know what I'm saying?

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.800
Like you grow, and like the conversation,

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.987
you have kids, you have like all that,

00:09:38.987 --> 00:09:41.110
you know, life happens.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.180
That's gotta be cool.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.010
- It was cool. It was cool
that all of us have married

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.080
and we have kids and grandchildren.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.340
You know, some of us
have grandchildren now,

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.330
and it's like, you know,

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.450
it's beautiful, you know.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.860
To get all the families
together and all of us together,

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.800
and you know, just love upon each other.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:07.360
- And you're like making so
many people happy on that stage.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.480
So, Alicia, like what are you grateful for

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.260
at this point in your life?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:15.360
- Oh, we're just grateful
to be healthy at this point.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:16.240
We know how many people

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.140
have gone through so many health scares

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.750
and lost so many people over the pandemic.

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:23.180
We're just grateful to have
each other and our health,

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.510
and our children are healthy, you know.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.343
And

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:30.460
today is just better than yesterday.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:31.487
- Yeah.
- Oh, and that's the goal!

00:10:31.487 --> 00:10:32.573
(audience clapping)

00:10:32.573 --> 00:10:33.477
That's the goal.

00:10:33.477 --> 00:10:36.340
That's a great, I'm gonna steal that.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.000
I'm like letting that sink in right now.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.850
I'm like, yes, that's
the goal, to have it,

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:41.410
and also better for our children.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.010
Well, it's very nice to have y'all here.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:43.843
- Thank you for having us.
- Thank you so much.

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:45.553
- We appreciate it so much.

00:10:45.553 --> 00:10:48.660
- You can see "Biography:
Bobby Brown" starting May 30th,

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.080
and "Bobby Brown: Every
Little Step", May 31st.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.040
Both on A&amp;E.

